":"nchandrappa","id":13372144,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMzcyMTQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13372144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nchandrappa","html_url":"https://github.com/nchandrappa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nchandrappa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nchandrappa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nchandrappa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nchandrappa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nchandrappa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nchandrappa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nchandrappa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nchandrappa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nchandrappa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-05-22T12:45:00Z","updated_at":"2020-05-22T12:45:00Z","body":"Basically `Spring-Data-Cassandra` is generating the DDL based on the `DataType.JSON` value in the YCQL java driver. Driver specifies the enum value  as `JSON` and not `JSONB `, hence Spring App throws the following error.\r\n```\r\nInvocation of init method failed; nested exception is org.springframework.data.cassandra.CassandraQuerySyntaxException: Query; CQL [CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS customer (address json, emailid text, id text, name text, PRIMARY KEY (id));]; Invalid SQL Statement. syntax error, unexpected JSON, expecting ')' or ','\r\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS customer (address json, emailid text, id text, name text, PRIMARY KEY (id));\r\n                                             ^^^^\r\n```\r\nWe'll need to fix the ENUM vaue in `DataType.java` to match the data type expected on the server side which is `JSONB`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/